00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,832
听：Reading the Numbers Carefully.

2
00:00:02,832 --> 00:00:05,664
跟读：Reading the Numbers Carefully.

3
00:00:05,664 --> 00:00:31,056
听：For a class project, Ben compared two fictional shopping centres. A chart showed that visits to Centre A rose from forty thousand to fifty thousand in one year. This was an increase of twenty-five per cent. Ben first wrote that visits had risen to twenty-five per cent, but his teacher asked him to check the units.

4
00:00:31,056 --> 00:00:56,448
跟读：For a class project, Ben compared two fictional shopping centres. A chart showed that visits to Centre A rose from forty thousand to fifty thousand in one year. This was an increase of twenty-five per cent. Ben first wrote that visits had risen to twenty-five per cent, but his teacher asked him to check the units.

5
00:00:56,448 --> 00:01:20,784
听：Centre B experienced a gradual decline before reaching a plateau. Its total revenue remained fairly stable because average spending increased. Ben learned that a trend in one measure did not necessarily describe the whole business. He needed an overview before listing individual figures.

6
00:01:20,784 --> 00:01:45,120
跟读：Centre B experienced a gradual decline before reaching a plateau. Its total revenue remained fairly stable because average spending increased. Ben learned that a trend in one measure did not necessarily describe the whole business. He needed an overview before listing individual figures.

7
00:01:45,120 --> 00:02:09,960
听：The proportion of visitors arriving by bicycle also changed. At Centre A, it rose from ten per cent to fifteen per cent, a rise of five percentage points. In relative terms, that was a fifty per cent increase. The two statements described the same change from different perspectives.

8
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:34,800
跟读：The proportion of visitors arriving by bicycle also changed. At Centre A, it rose from ten per cent to fifteen per cent, a rise of five percentage points. In relative terms, that was a fifty per cent increase. The two statements described the same change from different perspectives.

9
00:02:34,800 --> 00:03:03,408
听：Ben revised his report and removed unsupported explanations. The chart did not reveal why customers behaved differently, so he avoided inventing a cause. He compared the most noticeable features and checked every percentage. His final paragraph was shorter, but the figures were easier to understand and the comparisons were more precise.

10
